# a held job inside its safety margin gives DEADLINE_SOON; touch restores its TTR so the next reserve simply times out. The sleep sits just inside the 1s safety margin before the TTR (4s..5s) so a stalled machine has most of that window to spare; touch then leaves 5s.
@p send "put 0 0 5 1\r\nx\r\n"
@p recv
@h send "reserve\r\n"
@h recv
sleep 4200ms
@h send "reserve-with-timeout 0\r\n"
@h recv
@h send "touch 1\r\n"
@h recv
@h send "reserve-with-timeout 0\r\n"
@h recv
@h send "stats-job 1\r\n"
@h recv
